  bootwright / cluster exec
      Run a command over SSH on cluster nodes' Machines. By default, log in with the Machine's
      SSH identity. Select a different account with --ssh-user and its --ssh-id-file or
      --ssh-ask-password. Password prompts require a terminal and one target. An unproved host
      key requires interactive confirmation before SSH offers a credential. The exit status is
      the client's. Bootwright flags go before the command. Use -- before a flag-shaped first
      payload value to preserve it as data. After the first payload value, all remaining tokens
      belong to the payload. Each word reaches the remote command exactly as given: no shell on
      the Machine expands a glob, a variable, a pipe or a redirection in it. --shell runs the
      words as one script of the Machine's /bin/sh, where $name is the Machine's value. --var
      <name>=<value> sets $name in that script to a value from this host, quoted as data, so
      quote the script from your own shell and let it expand only the --var values; a value is
      visible in process listings, so never pass a secret. --sudo runs the command, or the
      whole script with its globs, through the Machine's sudo, which must not ask for a
      password. --name takes a comma-separated list, and each cluster runs the command on the
      Machine behind its administrator node. --node takes a comma-separated list and selects
      those nodes, by name then by FQDN, in every listed cluster that declares them. The
      command runs on every resolved Machine concurrently, at most eight at a time, each output
      line is prefixed by its Machine, and the exit status is the highest any client returned.
      For an OpenShiftCluster, the default is its first node in name order, and --node also
      accepts <role>-<ordinal> with a zero-based ordinal in that order (for example,
      controlPlane-0 or worker-0). External CephClusters are inapplicable.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster exec <command>... [flags]

  Command flags
      --name   Select comma-separated cluster names (required)
      --node   Select declared nodes by comma-separated name, then FQDN (default: each
               cluster's administrator node)
      --shell  Run the command as one script of the Machine's /bin/sh, which expands its
               variables, globs, pipes and redirections
      --sudo   Run the command through the Machine's sudo, without a password prompt
      --var    Set $<name> in the --shell script to a value from this host, as <name>=<value>
               (repeatable)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright cluster exec --context lab --name storage -- uname -a
